Actually, the words "rustproof", "erodeproof", "corrodeproof", and "fireproof"
all mean the same thing when you wish.  When you specify any of them, nethack
records that the item is erodeproof.  Then when you do an inventory (if they
are identified), then you see them as the appropriate kind of erodeproof.

So, if you wish for a 
  - fireproof fire brand 
  - rustproof fire brand
  - corrodeproof fire brand
  - erodeproof fire brand
what you get (if successful) is a erodeproof fire brand.  When it is 
listed, you see a rustproof Fire Brand.

The one bug I've noticed in this display procedure is for speed boots.
Even if the pair you have is erodeproof and identified, it still just 
lists as "speed boots", not "fireproof speed boots".  (You can verify 
that they are erodeproof by stepping into lava, and seeing them not burn).
I took a quick peek at the code, and can't see why this is.  Other boots
do identify correctly.  (note: nh 3.1.0 -- I haven't upgraded yet).
